      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Did some investigation! \n@{5f2d38467f57433511425209|full_name}'s post up above was made using \"IK 1.0\", which was the build that was live on May 18th. I asked them via Discord DM and they noted that there was no change in behavior between IK 1.0 and IK 2.0. This lines up with our expectation.\nIn short, **this hasn't changed with the release of IK 2.0**. I've confirmed this with engineers and recorded video/screenshots of IK 1.0. (We suspect people saying it *did* change were previously using client modifications. Don't break the rules. *smack*)\nWe'd consider this less a bug and more a \"refinement request\" without a straightforward answer, because if you rotate the hand to line up the index fingers, all of your other fingers are now angled out of alignment. This may not be desirable to people who are fine with the current implementation (and who also wouldn't come digging around on Canny to find a post to say \"no I like how it is right now\")\nAs such, I'm going to move this post to Feature Requests.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
